 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to the imposition of an occupancy tax\nin the town of DeWitt; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6507",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6507-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-zz-1, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6507\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to the imposition of an occu-\npancy tax in the town of DeWitt; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to authorize the town of DeWitt to impose an\noccupancy tax on persons occupying hotel and motel rooms in its juris-\ndiction.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend the Tax Law by adding a new section\n1202-zz-1, which would authorize the town of DeWitt to impose an occu-\npancy tax on persons occupying hotel and motel rooms in its jurisdic-\ntion.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect immediately and shall expire and be deemed repealed September 1,\n2025.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will authorize the town of DeWitt to impose an occupancy tax\nof up to two percent of the per diem rental rate upon persons occupying\nany room in any hotel or motel within its jurisdiction for the period\nextending to September 1, 2025. The town of DeWitt would utilize the\noccupancy tax revenue for specific line items in the annual town budget\ndedicated to the town's Willis Carrier Park and tourism infrastructure\nimprovements.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S.6149-B (Antonacci) - Referred to Investigations and Govern-\nment Operations.\n\n2017-18: S.8814 (DeFrancisco) - Referred to Investigations and Govern-\nment Operations.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed September 1, 2025.\n",
